    "media:imagetext": "Via PAN AMERICAN\nBETHEL O-\nFAIRBANKS\nCANADA\nSEATTLE\nONITED STATES\nSAN FRANCISCO\nHONOLULU\nMIDWAY 1.\nANGELES\nBROWNSVILLE\n• WAKE IS.\nSHANGHAI\nGUAM\nPAOFIC OCEAN\nMEXICO CIT\nVER pioneer aerial trade routes blazed by Lindbergh\nto the lands of the West Indies, Central and South\nAmerica, high above the age-old routes of Columbus,\nswash-buckling pirateers, of\nclipper ships of another generation, great Flying Clipper\nShips now speed along radio-guarded highways of the sky\nto thirty-three countries and colonies of the southern\nAmericas. Linking the New World and the Old, they\nspan the vast Pacific to Hawaii, the Philippines and China.\nWith a record unexcelled by any other form of trans-\nportation-for schedules maintained at 99.678% over\neight years-more than 750,000 passengers have flown\nmore than three hundred million miles—thirty million\npounds of mail and cargo have been carried-on these\nroutes that link the Americas, that span Alaska, the Pa-\ncific and far-off China, and cross the Atlantic to Bermuda.\nWherever you go \"via Pan American,\" you travel in\nthe finest equipment aviation science has produced. And,\n\"via Pan American,\" you travel with the supreme assur-\nance that your capable crew-and the 4,000 trained ex-\nperts along the airways—are in constant attendance on\nthe swift, sure flight of your airliner.\nFOR INFORMATION OR RESERVATIONS CALL\nAMERICAN AIRLINES, INC.\n512 West Sixth Street, Los Angeles\n6735 Hollywood Blvd., Hollywood\nTelephone MIchigan 8822\n(24-hour Service)\nPRINTED IN U.S.A.\nBOSTON\nNEW YORK\nO WASHINGTON\nAZORES\nMIAMI,\nHAVANA\nNASSAU\nKINGSTON\nBERMUDA\nATLANTIC OCEAN\nSAN JUAN\nPORT OF SPAIN\nSO OBOGOTA\nGUAYAQUIL\nBELENE\nUMA\nMANAOS\nSOUTH AMERICA\nIA PAZ\nRIO DE JANEIRO\nSANTIAGO d\n• MONTEVIDEO\nBUENOS AIRES\nRoutes of the\nFlying Clipper Ships\nWORLD'S STANDARD FOR AIR TRANSPORTATION",
